From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:26:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] VLAN: Set up a dynamic VLAN interface without its RTM_NEWLINK event

With CONFIG_FULL_DYNAMIC_VLAN, vlan_add_dynamic() creates the interface
of a dynamic VLAN. Only the RTM_NEWLINK event of that interface, through
vlan_event_receive(), then creates the bridge and the tagged interfaces
of the VLAN and adds the interface to the bridge. If the receive queue
of the VLAN netlink socket is full, the kernel drops the event, and
hostapd logs "VLAN: vlan_event_receive: recvfrom failed: No buffer
space available". The stations of the VLAN then have no path to the
bridge.

Call vlan_newlink() when the interface is created, as vlan_dynamic_add()
does for a static VLAN. The interface exists at that point, since
vlan_if_add() already sets it up. vlan_newlink() ignores the later
event for a VLAN that it configured.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/ap/vlan_init.c
+++ b/src/ap/vlan_init.c
@@ -227,9 +227,13 @@ struct hostapd_vlan * vlan_add_dynamic(s
 	if (vlan_if_add(hapd, n, 0)) {
 		hapd->conf->vlan = n->next;
 		os_free(n);
-		n = NULL;
+		return NULL;
 	}
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_FULL_DYNAMIC_VLAN
+	vlan_newlink(n->ifname, hapd);
+#endif /* CONFIG_FULL_DYNAMIC_VLAN */
+
 	return n;
 }
 
